// An augmented assignment to an indexed target reads it with `[]`, does the
// operation, and stores the result back with `[]=`: here `AddIntI` adds the `2`
// into r3. The container and index are read once, into r1 and r2, and copied
// as the arguments of both calls. The assignment's `()` isn't used, so nothing
// makes it.
// compile: stdlib
let values = [1]; values[0] += 2;
